# Frontend Patterns

Coding patterns for building user interfaces. Applies to React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, or plain HTML/CSS/JS. Examples use React/JSX syntax for illustration — adapt to your framework. IF your project has a UI, apply these patterns.

> All numeric values in this file are `[DEFAULT]` — adjust per project.

---

## Component Structure

- **One primary export per file** — small helper components tightly coupled to the main component can live in the same file (e.g., a `Row` helper inside `Table.tsx`), but don't export them separately
- **Colocate related code** — styles, tests, and types near the component
- **File length** — follow the tiered limits in `code-formatting.md` (simple components ~200, complex modules up to 1500)
- **Props over internal state** for configurable components
- **Composition over inheritance** — build from smaller pieces

---

## Responsive Design (Mobile-First)

**Default: every page should work from 375px to 4K.** Exception: specialized data-dense views and data-heavy tables (complex grids, analytics, multi-column reports) may target 768px+ minimum with a "best on desktop" note.

- Start with mobile layout, add complexity for larger screens
- Prefer relative units (rem, %, vw/vh) for layout. px is fine for hairlines, shadows, and specific design tokens.
- Breakpoints: 640px (sm), 768px (md), 1024px (lg), 1280px (xl)
- Test on: iPhone SE (375px), iPad (768px), Desktop (1440px)
- Touch targets: minimum 44x44px on mobile
- Avoid horizontal scroll on content pages. Data tables, Gantt charts, and code blocks may use horizontal scroll with proper scroll indicators.
- Navigation: hamburger/drawer on mobile, full nav on desktop

---

## State Management

**Principle:** Classify state by ownership and lifetime — where it originates and how long it lives determines where it should be stored.

[REFERENCE] Common state categories:

- **Local state** for: form inputs, toggles, modals, dropdowns, UI-only concerns
- **Global state** for: current user, permissions, theme, app-wide data shared across routes
- **Server state** for: API data — use a caching fetch hook (SWR/React Query/equivalent)
- **URL state** for: filters, pagination, active tabs — anything the user might share/bookmark

**Rules:**
- Avoid duplicating server data in global state — use caching fetch hooks (SWR/React Query) as the source of truth
- Form state belongs in local/component state by default. Multi-step wizards or cross-page drafts may use global or URL state.
- Derive computed values — don't store them separately
- Clear global state on session end

---

## Data Fetching

- **Centralized fetch hook** with built-in caching, revalidation, and error handling
- **Loading state** for every async operation (no blank screens)
- **Error state** with retry button for failed requests
- **Optimistic updates** for instant-feeling mutations (revert on failure)
- **Prefetch** on hover/focus for likely navigation targets
- **Deduplicate** concurrent identical requests

---

## Loading States

**Every async UI should handle three states: loading, success, error.** Stale-while-revalidate patterns (show cached data + background refresh) count as handling all three.

- **Page loads**: Full skeleton matching content shape
- **Button actions**: Spinner inside button + disabled state
- **Inline updates**: Subtle loading indicator near the affected area
- **Transitions**: Smooth fade/slide between states (no jumps)

**Never:**
- Show a blank white page while loading
- Show content then jump when data arrives (layout shift)
- Use a full-page spinner for partial updates

---

## Forms

- **Controlled inputs** — state drives the value, always
- **Credential/security fields** (username, password, etc.): validate on **blur** and on **submit**
- **Other fields:** validate on **submit** only (avoid noisy inline validation)
- **Errors:** inline below field only — **focus first** invalid field on failed submit (no top-of-form summary block)
- **Disabled submit** while request is in progress
- **Mutation feedback** — MUST give user-visible success; **channel test:** cart/add/remove → toast; settings/password/profile → inline success OK
- **Unsaved changes** warning when closing **modals/drawers** with dirty forms
- **Auto-focus** first field on page load / modal open
- **Keyboard support** — Enter to submit, Tab between fields

---

## Toast / Notifications

Every mutation should have feedback (toast or inline per channel test above).

**API errors:** map to form fields when possible; toast only for non-field or unexpected failures.

**Accessibility:** toast region MUST use `aria-live` (polite for success, assertive for errors).

- **Success**: Auto-dismissing notification — `[DEFAULT]` 3 seconds
- **Error**: Persistent notification (stays longer or until dismissed) — `[DEFAULT]` 8 seconds
- **Info**: Brief notification for informational messages
- **Position**: Pick one position and be consistent across the app — `[DEFAULT]` top-right or bottom-right
- **Stack**: Multiple notifications stack vertically, not overlap
- **Colors/styling**: Follow your design system tokens (see `ui-design-system.md`), not hardcoded colors

---

## Theming / Dark Mode (IF your project supports theming or multiple visual themes)

Patterns for implementing theme support when your project includes it:

- **CSS variables** for all colors — avoid hardcoding hex values (makes theming easier even without dark mode)
- **System preference** detection on first load (`prefers-color-scheme`)
- **Manual toggle** that overrides system preference
- **Persist choice** in localStorage
- **No flash** on page load (apply theme before paint via script in `<head>`)
- **Test both modes** — no invisible text, missing borders, or broken contrast

---

## Accessibility (MUST in touched files)

Apply to every file the agent opens or edits for UI — not a whole-app backfill mandate.

- **Semantic HTML**: Use `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<form>`, `<label>` — not div-for-everything
- **Labels on every input**: Visible label or aria-label (no placeholder-only inputs)
- **Focus management**: Visible focus ring on all interactive elements
- **Keyboard navigation**: Every feature usable without mouse (Tab, Enter, Escape)
- **Color contrast**: 4.5:1 minimum for text, 3:1 for large text/icons
- **Alt text** on meaningful images (empty alt for decorative)
- **aria-live** for dynamic content updates (toast, loading status)
- **Modals/drawers:** focus trap while open; restore focus to trigger on close
- **Icon-only controls:** accessible name (`aria-label`); tooltip SHOULD supplement, not replace the name
- **Destructive actions:** danger styling + confirm before irreversible delete
- **Escape key** closes modals/dropdowns
- **Skip navigation** link for keyboard users
- **Reduced motion**: MUST respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — provide static alternative
- **Empty states**: MUST show message ± action when lists/grids have zero results — not blank UI
- **Error boundaries**: PREFER per route/feature segment — not only a root error page

---

## Animations

- **Purposeful only** — animation must communicate something (entry, exit, state change)
- **Fast**: 100-200ms for UI feedback (hover, toggle), 200-300ms for page transitions — use your project's defined duration tokens consistently
- **Ease curves**: ease-out for entries, ease-in for exits
- **No animation** for reduced-motion preference
- **Never block interaction** waiting for animation to finish
- **Consistent** — same type of elements animate the same way everywhere

